----- Original Message ----
From: Paul Thacker <lennier_of_the_minbari@yahoo.com>
To: ballyalley@yahoogroups.com
Sent: Saturday, April 26, 2008 10:49:43 PM
Subject: [ballyalley] 300 baud Flying Ace

                So, I managed to get my 300 baud interface back together no worse for
the wear (though no better, either), so now I can post about a curious
finding.  As you may recall, I successfully archived the vast majority
of programs on the WaveMakers master tapes, but one I couldn't get
working no matter how hard I tried was the 300 baud version of Flying
Ace.  I kept getting errors on lines 260, 310, and 380, which pretty
much ensured it couldn't work.  I figured the tape had gone bad in
these spots, so I was happy to learn that Mike White had a commercial
version of the tape.  Well, I've tried to archive it, and it seems
like the same code.  In fact, it seems too much like the same code,
because it has errors on lines 260, 310, and 380!  Could it really be
that the master tape went bad long ago?  Wouldn't someone have
noticed?  Does anyone remember ever playing the 300 baud version of
Flying Ace?

I think it's pretty unlikely I'm going to be able to archive this one
directly from tape.  Kenn, are you still interested in fixing this? 
It may well be as simple as just correcting three single-character
